# Completing config/docker.config's requests.
#
# config/docker.config is part of the port's patch stack and is merged
# verbatim; a few of its lines cannot land as written on this tree because
# the symbol they configure needs a companion the file does not set — and
# olddefconfig then drops the request SILENTLY (no "# ... is not set"
# marker; the line simply vanishes from the .config, and only a strict
# per-symbol audit like ci/cfg-check.py sees it).  One companion per line:
#
#   NET_CLS_CGROUP -> needs NET_SCHED.  net/sched/Kconfig gates the whole
#     classifier menu behind `menuconfig NET_SCHED`; with it off the symbol
#     is invisible and the request drops.  (Optional tier for docker.
#     NET_SCHED itself is the standard "QoS and/or fair queueing" switch
#     every general-purpose kernel ships.)
#   NFT_FIB_INET   -> needs NFT_FIB_IPV6.  Its Kconfig is
#     `depends on NF_TABLES_INET && NFT_FIB_IPV4 && NFT_FIB_IPV6`, and
#     docker.config sets the IPv4 variant only, so the inet one dropped.
#
# Kept out of config/ so the port's file stays byte-identical to the stack;
# delete a line here the day the port's fragment grows the companion itself
# (cfg-check.py will keep passing either way).
CONFIG_NET_SCHED=y
CONFIG_NET_CLS_CGROUP=y
CONFIG_NFT_FIB_IPV6=y